 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items?limit=20&cursor=...` → `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": "..."}`:
+  items are ordered by `id`. `limit` is optional (1–100, default 20); pass
+  the previous response's `next_cursor` unchanged to fetch the next page.
+  `next_cursor` is `null` on the last page. Invalid limits or cursors return
+  status 400 with an `error` body.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
